.TH MU2EDAQ-DATAFORMAT-VIEWER.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer.py \- decode Mu2e ROC packets from YAML definitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.py
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ formats_dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A PyQt6 window that shows raw packet bytes as a field-by-field table
(name, word, bits, hex, binary, decimal, decoded value) using the packet
definitions in
.IR formats/*.yaml
(see
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-formats.yaml (5)).
Bytes come from typed hex, a binary file
.RB ( "Load file" ),
or the network.
.PP
Each field is read from 16-bit word
.B word
of the data, starting at the byte offset in the
.B Offset
box, and bits
.BR bits .
Words are assembled
.B big-endian
(first byte high) unless
.B Little-endian words
is ticked.
The DTC software in artdaq-core-mu2e reads the same buffers little-endian
(byte 0 is the low byte of word 0), so tick the box for DTC DMA dumps and
artdaq fragments.
A field whose word lies beyond the data is omitted from the table without
any warning.
Fields with a
.B fixed_value
are shown green when they match and red when they do not.
.B Auto-detect type
reads the packet type from bits 7:4 of word 1 and selects the matching
format from a built-in table (types 0x0\(en0x8); data payload packets carry
no type field, so detection is meaningless for them.
.PP
.B Network input.
.B Start listening
binds the
.B Port
on
.B 0.0.0.0
(all interfaces), TCP or UDP as selected.
For TCP each connection is read until the peer closes it and the whole byte
stream is shown as one packet; there is no size or time limit and no peer
filtering.
For UDP each datagram (up to 65536 bytes) is one packet.
Every received packet replaces the display and triggers auto-detect.
The listener is not started automatically.
.PP
.B Discovery.
If
.B mu2edaq_discovery
is importable, a responder announcing app
.BR dataformat\-viewer ,
scheme
.BR tcp ,
and the configured port is started at launch, before and regardless of
listening.
.PP
.B Known defect:
with
.B Word size
set to 2 or 4 bytes the hex panel is rewritten as multi-byte tokens that the
parser rejects, and the table stays empty with
.BR "Parse error" .
Keep word size at 1 byte.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Configuration file; see
.BR mu2e\-viewer.yaml (5).
Without it the first of
.IR ./mu2e\-viewer.yaml ,
.IR ./config.yaml ,
.IR ./config/mu2e\-viewer.yaml ,
.I ./config/config.yaml
relative to the
.B current directory
is used.
A named file that does not exist is fatal.
.TP
.I formats_dir
Directory of format YAML files; overrides
.BR formats_dir .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_LISTEN
Overrides
.B viewer.port
(set by the control-room launcher).
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/mu2e\-viewer.yaml
Shipped configuration
.RB ( formats_dir: ../formats ).
.TP
.I formats/*.yaml
Packet definitions;
.I packet_type_index.yaml
is skipped.
.TP
.I test/test.dat
20-byte big-endian sample heartbeat.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The Qt event loop's exit code, normally 0.
1 if PyYAML or PyQt6 cannot be imported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
cd ~/mu2edaq\-main/mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer
\&./venv/bin/python mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.py
\&./venv/bin/python mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.py \-\-config config/mu2e\-viewer.yaml
mu2e_send \-f test/test.dat localhost 7755      # after Start listening
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run it from the checkout directory, or pass
.B \-\-config
or
.IR formats_dir ;
from any other directory no formats are found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-sender.py (1),
.BR mu2e_send (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.sh (1),
.BR mu2e\-viewer.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-formats.yaml (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
